---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import JobsHeroVideo from '../components/JobsHeroVideo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Job Opportunities"
  description="Pathways into space careers: engineering, mission operations, science, and software roles."
>
  <section class="page-home-hero">
    <JobsHeroVideo />
    <div class="page-home-hero-inner">
      <p class="page-home-hero-eyebrow">Careers</p>
      <h1 class="page-home-hero-heading">Job opportunities in space</h1>
      <p class="page-home-hero-lead">
        Engineering, software, operations, and science teams that turn missions from concept into flight.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-24 md:px-8">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Mission context"
      title="Where careers open up"
      subtitle="A practical overview of where space-industry jobs exist, what teams look for, and how to build a strong entry path."
    />

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">Common role tracks</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Aerospace and mechanical engineering (structures, thermal, mechanisms)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Avionics and embedded software (flight computers, sensors, controls)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Mission operations (planning, console ops, telemetry, anomaly response)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Data and science roles (remote sensing, modeling, payload analysis)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Manufacturing and integration (test, QA, system integration)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">What helps candidates stand out</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Evidence of shipped work: code, design reviews, test plans, flight/robotics projects</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Strong systems thinking: requirements, interfaces, failure modes, trade-offs</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Clear communication under constraints (status updates, risk framing, handoffs)</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> Internship/co-op or lab experience with real timelines and verification gates</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-nebula/20 bg-nebula/5 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Where to look</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">
        Start with official career portals (national agencies, major primes, launch companies, smallsat startups, and
        mission-ops contractors). University labs and open-source aerospace communities are also strong gateways to
        practical team experience.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
        Tip: tailor your resume to one role family at a time (for example, mission ops vs flight software) and show
        project outcomes, not just tool lists.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
